s://scontent-sea5-2.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/499620559_1417842779810782_3827818758806445771_n.png?_nc_cat=104&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=yj-doBXcCcIQ7kNvwHdB1ze&_nc_oc=AdrWNPw7WxVf7wvuvGYiZPsENCz3eTrpCq4sgkzzPifgdB0pJjfHbTEtVPz9cTP_wpQ&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-sea5-2.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f20f&oh=00_AQRQweJpqf8UaCGWMqyhvFiJUuqT38dq1j6klbGg6eL-UA&oe=6AFC72C6"}], "video_trailer": null, "video_trailer_thumbnail": null, "display_name": "Safe Steps", "keywords": [], "long_description": "Safe Steps is a Virtual Reality application designed to teach Indian school-going children essential traffic and road-safety practices through immersive, interactive experiences. It helps children understand safe road crossing, traffic signals, pedestrian etiquette, hazard awareness, and responsible behavior in realistic virtual road environments.\n\nThrough scenario-based VR simulations, children can observe traffic, make decisions, and learn from their actions in a safe and controlled environment. The application turns conventional safety education into an engaging and memorable learning experience while allowing students to practice real-world situations without physical risk.\n\nSafe Steps demonstrates the use of immersive technology for meaningful educational and social impact, helping schools introduce practical road-safety awareness in an engaging and technology-driven format.", "short_description": "Virtual Reality Application for Traffic Safety Education in Indian School Going Children, Safe Steps uses immersive VR to teach kids road-crossing behaviour, pedestrian etiquette, and traffic-rule awareness turning safety education into an engaging, memorable experience rather than a one-time lecture."}]}, "developer_name": null, "developer_privacy_policy_url": "https://safesteps.info/privacy-policy.html", "developer_terms_of_service_url": null, "publisher_name": "Yogeshwar Navandar", "support_website_url": null, "website_url": "https://safesteps.info/"